abstract: Bao mian lan chu [Preventing and averting illness] is an 1867 Chinese medical
  and everyday-health booklet by Frederick Porter Smith. Bodleian Sinica 2044 is catalogued
  as published in Hankow; the title page names Baoshan jushe as block holder. Its
  discussions of housing, diet, mental and physical activity, cleanliness and medical
  conditions, linked with Christian vocabulary, support research on medical translation,
  missionary publishing and late-Qing everyday life. Based on 21 images, the dataset
  provides TXT, JSON and TEI XML for 36 designated physical faces, with uncertainties
  and source mappings. The provisional AI transcription includes selected source-image
  corrections; full human double collation and expert review have not been performed.
